; setline_integer_sample_out_of_domain: the integer domain starts at 0.
;
; QUI-1150 settled the integer domain as {0, ..., k-1}, where k is the
; number of values. Under the signed centred reading it replaced, k = 3 gave
; {-3, ..., 2} and the write below was legal -- integer_alloc asserted
; exactly that, and argued for it at length in its comments.
;
; So this vector is the shape decision made executable. A check that merely
; rejects something out of range would pass with either reading; only the
; lower bound at 0 distinguishes them.

PUSH 4
PUSH 3
XSMX r0          ; integer sample, k = 3, domain {0, 1, 2}

PUSH 1
PUSH -1          ; below the domain; legal under the old centred reading
SETLINE r0
HALT
